; Frame call list gate: RET while the list is not complete, NOP when it is
;
; The first byte of the frame call list runner (#R$BDDB), which it falls into when it is a NOP. It is a flag and an
; entry point at once. Observed over a frame: #R$A5DB (the end of the game frame, when the frame list is complete)
; stores 0 here, so a CALL to this address runs the list; #R$BDDB stores $C9 (RET) as the first thing it does, so a
; second call does nothing until the next list is complete. #R$86B9 also stores $C9 when a room is entered. The main
; loop (#R$85FC) and the cutscene loops ($8832, $88DE, #R$8869) wait until the byte is zero and then CALL it.
; .
; The byte is not data to read as a number only: the same address is read with LD A,(nn) by those loops.
@label=FrameListGate
c$BDDA RET           ; RET until the list is complete; 0 (NOP) when it is
